<br />This mod helps Stardew Valley run smoother on some PCs by changing how your computer shares its CPU power with the game.
<br />
<br />[b][color=#00ff00]What it does[/color][/b][list]
<br />[*]When you [b]start the game[/b], the mod sets Stardew Valley to use [b]every CPU core except “CPU 0”[/b].
<br />[*]This matches the manual “Task Manager fix” some players use:
<br />[list]
<br />[*]Open Task Manager → Details → Stardew Valley → Set affinity → [b]uncheck CPU 0[/b] → OK
<br />…but the mod does it automatically for you.[/list][/list][b][color=#00ff00]Focus / Alt-Tab behavior (smart switching)[/color][/b][list]
<br />[*]When the game window is [b]focused[/b] (you’re playing): it applies the “exclude CPU 0” setting.
<br />[*]When the game window is [b]unfocused[/b] (you alt-tab): it [b]restores the game to normal[/b].
<br />[*]When you return to the game: it [b]re-applies[/b] the setting again.
<br />[/list]
<br />
<br />[img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/1303/images/40439/40439-1766283651-1591135524.png[/img]﻿
<br />[b][color=#00ff00]Easy settings (optional)
<br />[/color][/b]
<br />[list]
<br />[*]Turn the mod on/off
<br />[*]Choose how cores are used (recommended default is already set)
<br />[*]Toggle whether it restores settings when you alt-tab
<br />[/list][b][color=#00ff00]Notes[/color][/b][list]
<br />[*][b]Windows only.[/b]
<br />[*]This won’t boost FPS for everyone, but for some players it reduces stutter and makes the game feel more stable.
<br />[/list][b][color=#ffff00]You can also manually trigger it each game session by going to Task manager
<br />[/color][/b]
